flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J12_run.log:53908:+HARNESS: initial data-page enable exposed DUT/Spike memory-map mismatch. DUT executes at PC 0 while ELF/Spike use 0x1000; data symbols were 0x1000-based. Fix: `tb_riscvdv_lockstep.v` subtracts ELF_BASE=0x1000 for D-memory indexing, and `firmware.lds` includes riscv-dv `.region*` data sections in the loaded image.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J12_run.log:53910:+REAL-DUT residual outside J12 scope: RV32IMC exploratory run then exposed M-unit/result association mismatches (e.g. seed 2026061201 PC 0x1478 `rem s10,s8,gp`: raw Spike x26=0, DUT x26=0x472816d0). Not fixed here; J12 generation moved to RV32IC per "M/mul-div may stay as-is".
