codex
I found the behavioral bug: data misalign traps redirect the PC, but the EX/MEM to EX/WB flush condition only treated IRQ/sync-trap/MRET as WB redirects. That lets the next wrong-path instruction advance on the same trap cycle, which is why the “aligned byte” marker reappears after the first trap.
