codex
There is a third root cause in the same regression path: the trap target is `0x5c`, but the handler starts at `0x58`. The core skips the first handler instruction (`csrr mepc`), so it writes garbage back to `mepc` and restarts the program. I’m checking whether that comes from CSR forwarding, `mtvec`, or IF redirect warmup alignment.
