flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:14:ROLE: Codex EXECUTOR (gpt-5.5), PL=Claude. design_id=cpu_m1 (RV32IMC_Zicsr_Zifencei, M-mode). OSS+riscv-none-elf-gcc; -s danger-full-access. Spike GOLDEN. report-faithfully: classify each divergence (real-DUT vs harness) with evidence; never hide; never mask a real DUT bug via the comparator.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:16:CONTEXT: After J9-J13, full RV32IMC (load/store + branch/jump + M) runs CLEAN on riscv-dv lockstep (5 seeds, CSR still OFF). Harness flow/v2_pipeline/phase_03_09_riscvdv_lockstep/; comparator flow/v2_pipeline/lib/spike_commit.py.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:18:GOAL J14: ENABLE CSR instructions + synchronous traps, get the lockstep clean. Scope = the M1's SUPPORTED Zicsr CSRs + M-mode trap path. EXPLICITLY keep async INTERRUPTS OFF for now (timing injection won't match Spike — separate later wave).
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:20:KEY CSR-lockstep rules (do these right, do NOT fake):
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:21:1. TIMING CSRs are fundamentally DUT!=Spike (mcycle/mcycleh, minstret/minstreth, time/cycle): the DUT counts real wait/stall cycles, Spike does not. So a `csrr` of a timing CSR legitimately differs. Handle by EXCLUDING timing-CSR read results from the wdata comparison (mark them as do-not-compare), NOT by faking equality. Document which CSRs are excluded and WHY. Non-timing CSR reads/writes (mstatus/mie/mtvec/mepc/mcause/mscratch/mip etc.) MUST still be compared exactly.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:22:2. Constrain riscv-dv to only generate accesses to CSRs the M1 actually implements (no unsupported CSRs unless both DUT and Spike trap identically). Synchronous traps (illegal instr, ecall, ebreak) + mret should be enabled and lockstepped (mepc/mcause/mtval + resume).
