flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54021:+# ADR-0010: CSR State and Synchronous Trap Lockstep
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54027:+J14 enabled Zicsr lockstep against Spike for the M1 M-mode CSR subset. The
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54028:+first active CSR sweep exposed real DUT state mismatches:
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54032:+- A back-to-back `csrrw mscratch` / `csrr mscratch` read old DUT CSR state.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54039:+sync-trap continuation cannot yet be included in the riscv-dv lockstep stream.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54042:+Implement the M-mode CSR behavior needed for exact non-timing CSR comparison:
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54045:+2. Forward pending CSR writes to following CSR reads in EX/MEM and same-cycle
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J14_run.log:54047:+3. Convert synchronous exceptions to precise trap entry: save exception PC in
