flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J9_run.log:18:BUG (see docs/reports/bug_xbound_0001/findings.md): riscv-dv seed 2026060801 — DUT & Spike agree commits 0-3 then DUT decodes a LEGAL `addi x31,x31,0xc` @pc=0x0e as illegal and traps; Spike retires it. A compressed c.li@0x4 shifts alignment to odd half-word, so pc 0x6/0xa/0xe are CONSECUTIVE cross-boundary (high-half) 32-bit instructions. Hypothesis: the lab08e residue/cross_assemble pre-fetch (IP/cpu_m1/rtl/pipeline_v2/ch2_lab08e/core.v ~lines 90-265: upcoming_cross / at_cross_boundary / cross_assemble / residue + ifu.v) handles 1 cross-boundary but does NOT set up residue for the NEXT one while consuming the current -> a RUN of cross-boundary 32-bit instrs mis-assembles the 3rd.
flow/v2_pipeline/phase_05_leader/J9_run.log:21:1. CONFIRM root cause: reproduce seed 2026060801 (flow/v2_pipeline/phase_03_09_riscvdv_lockstep, ./run_riscvdv_lockstep.py --start-seed 2026060801 --seeds 1). Add temporary internal probes (or a focused tb) to dump, at the cycle if_pc==0x0e: instr_assembled, cross_assemble, residue, cur_half_lo/hi, is_comp_*, at_cross_boundary, upcoming_cross, i_mem_rdata, i_mem_addr. Show that instr_assembled @0x0e != 0x00cf8f93 (mis-assembled). Write the evidence.
